A_556 - Personally, I advise against procreating if you're not in good health. Having damaged body parts (poor bones, chronically damaged internal organs) can lead to problems in your offspring. Bone integrity, in particular, is important for using computer tools or making certain assessments without errors. Otherwise, when possible, the only alternative solution is to double-check what you've typed, for example, two or three times to remove any inevitable errors. Furthermore, I generally advise against using a computer if you have health problems, as it could lead to errors or problems spreading both online and to the surrounding environment or computer-generated material.